00:29:44,620 --> 00:29:48,960
We now return to Warplanes of World War II on Modern Marvels.

383
00:29:48,961 --> 00:30:01,020
To defeat Adolf Hitler, it was essential that the Allies crippled the factories of the Nazi

384
00:30:01,021 --> 00:30:06,340
war machine.

385
00:30:06,341 --> 00:30:14,640
Britain's Royal Air Force mounted massive nighttime bombing attacks.

386
00:30:14,641 --> 00:30:20,640
America's eight therefore stage daring daylight raids.

387
00:30:20,641 --> 00:30:24,480
The raids took a deadly toll on both sides.

388
00:30:24,481 --> 00:30:29,600
As Allied bombers struck deeper and deeper into the heart of Germany, going far beyond

389
00:30:29,601 --> 00:30:34,880
the range of their escort fighters, German interceptors brought down a heartbreaking

390
00:30:34,881 --> 00:30:43,920
number of planes.

391
00:30:43,921 --> 00:30:54,660
One out of every three B-7 teams was lost or damaged beyond repair.

392
00:30:54,661 --> 00:31:01,020
The Allies needed a faster, deadlier escort, one that could go the distance with the bombers

393
00:31:01,021 --> 00:31:07,040
and outfight Germany's best fighters.

394
00:31:07,041 --> 00:31:12,700
The need would be met by a company that had never even built a fighter plane, North American

395
00:31:12,701 --> 00:31:13,535
aviation.

396
00:31:13,536 --> 00:31:20,860
In the spring of 1940, North American got an urgent request from Great Britain.

397
00:31:22,060 --> 00:31:27,480
Desperate for fighters, Britain asked for bids on 100 P-40s, airplanes designed nearly

398
00:31:27,481 --> 00:31:28,716
five years earlier.

399
00:31:28,717 --> 00:31:33,400
Dutch Kindleberger, North American's president, feared that the outdated

400
00:31:33,401 --> 00:31:40,340
P-40 couldn't hold its own against faster German aircraft. I'll talk to Dutch about

401
00:31:40,341 --> 00:31:44,260
the possibility of designing an airplane of our own, a fighter.

402
00:31:44,261 --> 00:31:45,940
And I knew that we couldn't

403
00:31:45,941 --> 00:31:49,960
get a contract from the Air Corps because we hadn't built one.

404
00:31:51,300 --> 00:31:52,949
But Britain was desperate.

405
00:31:52,950 --> 00:31:56,880
When North American proposed building a new fighter, the Brits

406
00:31:56,881 --> 00:31:59,840
ordered 320 of them sight unseen.

407
00:32:03,060 --> 00:32:08,680
North American got the go-ahead in April of 1940, two days after Germany invaded Norway.

408
00:32:10,340 --> 00:32:15,000
The fighter's official designation was the P-51.

409
00:32:15,960 --> 00:32:19,260
Its name coined by the Brits was the Mustang.

410
00:32:21,220 --> 00:32:25,460
North American had just 100 days to produce the prototype,

411
00:32:25,760 --> 00:32:28,280
an unheard of schedule for a new design.

412
00:32:29,180 --> 00:32:32,620
Adding to the pressure were the plane's revolutionary features.

413
00:32:33,820 --> 00:32:38,120
A thin, streamlined wing and an innovative radiator

414
00:32:38,121 --> 00:32:43,200
whose jet-like exhaust added some 30 miles an hour to the plane's top speed.

415
00:32:47,280 --> 00:32:53,120
As the plane took shape, Hitler provided a grim reminder of what was at stake.

416
00:32:53,740 --> 00:32:59,020
He launched a fierce airborne assault on Britain, the prelude to an invasion.

417
00:33:08,120 --> 00:33:13,120
Day and night the Germans pounded away.

418
00:33:13,121 --> 00:33:20,120
Their backs to the wall, the outnumbered and outgunned pilots of the Royal Air Force,

419
00:33:20,121 --> 00:33:27,120
the thin blue line they recalled, beat back wave after wave of German attackers.

420
00:33:38,120 --> 00:33:45,120
But the battle had stretched the thin blue line perilously close to breaking.

421
00:33:45,121 --> 00:33:48,120
The Mustang was needed more than ever.

422
00:33:48,121 --> 00:33:53,120
At North American, work continued at a fever pitch.

423
00:33:53,121 --> 00:33:59,120
But suddenly, a disastrous problem loomed, not with the Mustang's exotic design,

424
00:33:59,121 --> 00:34:06,120
but with North American's own workers, a wildcat strike by the local union demanding higher pay.

425
00:34:06,121 --> 00:34:14,611
This is a very controversial strike because there's some evidence that the local union did have leaders that either belonged to the Communist Party or at least were

426
00:34:14,612 --> 00:34:16,320
influenced by Communist ideology.

427
00:34:16,920 --> 00:34:21,700
And so therefore it became a real lightning rod for the debate over communism at the time.

428
00:34:22,140 --> 00:34:27,240
As the strike went on, eventually Roosevelt brought in the army to break the strike.

429
00:34:27,680 --> 00:34:29,820
And again, this was quite shocking to the labor movement.

430
00:34:29,821 --> 00:34:39,320
The president's strong stance worked, and soon Mustang fighters took to the skies at speeds approaching 400 miles an hour.

431
00:34:43,420 --> 00:34:46,660
But the Mustang was just getting warmed up.

432
00:34:47,180 --> 00:34:54,460
In 1942, the Mustang's General Motors engine was replaced by a powerful Rolls-Royce engine called the Merlin.

433
00:34:54,461 --> 00:35:00,100
I'll never forget when the flight test came in for speed.

434
00:35:00,540 --> 00:35:07,000
They had level flight speed at 25,000 feet, 443 miles an hour.

435
00:35:08,580 --> 00:35:12,360
It could outfly any plane at Hitler's Air Force.

436
00:35:13,400 --> 00:35:18,380
The Mustang's performance swiftly earned it the reputation as the best fighter in Europe.

437
00:35:18,381 --> 00:35:26,040
and with auxiliary fuel tanks its range stretched to more than 2,000 miles

438
00:35:26,041 --> 00:35:30,080
enough to reach the most distant targets in Germany.

439
00:35:31,460 --> 00:35:36,660
P-51 was a type of airplane would do almost anything you ask it to

440
00:35:36,661 --> 00:35:42,780
from 35,000 feet down to what we call the deck, down to ground level.

441
00:35:43,320 --> 00:35:47,400
We began to fly these missions in P-47s.

442
00:35:48,380 --> 00:35:55,440
In June of 1944, we switched over to the P-51C.

443
00:35:56,880 --> 00:36:01,680
It was almost like climbing out of a Mack truck into a Rolls Royce.

444
00:36:03,100 --> 00:36:08,200
North American was swamped with orders and expanded dramatically to meet the demand.

445
00:36:09,620 --> 00:36:14,200
In three plants, we peaked out at about 105,000 or 110,000 people.

446
00:36:14,201 --> 00:36:19,300
Big factory at Kansas City, Kansas, and another in Dallas, Texas.

447
00:36:20,540 --> 00:36:28,300
By the fourth Mustang model, the P-51D, with its distinctive bubble canopy, demand had skyrocketed.

448
00:36:29,240 --> 00:36:32,800
Nearly 8,000 of them galloped off the assembly lines.

449
00:36:34,980 --> 00:36:38,520
The Luftwaffe could not withstand the stampede.

450
00:36:39,160 --> 00:36:47,360
Mustang soon ruled the sky, shooting down nearly 5,000 enemy aircraft and destroying another 5,000 on the ground.

451
00:36:50,780 --> 00:36:53,600
We started out by doing bomber escort.

452
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:55,280
We did dive bombing.

453
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:59,520
The Mustang, of course, was a tremendous dive bombing airplane.

454
00:36:59,900 --> 00:37:05,980
Not only to mention its speed, but it had the capability to carry two 1,000-pound bombs,

455
00:37:05,981 --> 00:37:08,700
which in those days was a pretty good bomb load.

456
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:14,140
Without a doubt, the Mustang was the best prop-driven aircraft of World War II.

457
00:37:16,280 --> 00:37:20,400
The Mustang became the dominant fighter in the skies over Europe.

458
00:37:22,300 --> 00:37:26,440
But half a world away, in the skies above the Pacific,

459
00:37:27,040 --> 00:37:32,460
that distinction belonged to a fighter plane from a place called the Iron Works.

